# wpa_supplicant 2.9 build config — PSK-only, nl80211, no external crypto.
#
# Used by tools/mkrootfs.sh, which copies this file to .config in the extracted
# source tree inside the chroot. It is a tracked asset rather than a heredoc in
# the script so that it can be reviewed, diffed and tested on its own.
#
# Why 2.9 and not 2.10: 2.10 advertises RSN replay counters the MT7668 vendor
# driver does not implement, so every AP deauths with reason 2 — which looks
# exactly like a wrong passphrase. See docs/net.md.
# Why build it at all: no Alpine branch from v3.16 up ships 2.9, and borrowing
# v3.15's package would drag a 2023 binary and its libnl3 into a 3.20 rootfs.
#
# Two traps, both found by actually building it:
#   * 2.9 selects its crypto objects from CONFIG_TLS/CONFIG_CRYPTO, but the
#     Makefile does not pass -DCONFIG_CRYPTO_INTERNAL for this combination, so
#     sha1-internal.c compiles to nothing and the link dies on `sha1_vector`.
#     mkrootfs.sh builds with EXTRA_CFLAGS=-DCONFIG_CRYPTO_INTERNAL for that.
#   * The driver switch is CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211 in 2.9; CONFIG_DRV_NL80211 is
#     the newer spelling and is silently ignored here, producing a supplicant
#     that lists no drivers and fails at runtime instead of at build time.
#
# Net effect: no D-Bus, no wext, no EAP, no TLS library. The binary needs libc
# and libnl-3 only, and was 465 KiB stripped on x86_64 when this was written.

CONFIG_DRIVER_NL80211=y
CONFIG_LIBNL32=y
CONFIG_CTRL_IFACE=y
CONFIG_TLS=none
CONFIG_CRYPTO=internal
CONFIG_INTERNAL_SHA1=y
CONFIG_INTERNAL_MD5=y
CONFIG_INTERNAL_AES=y
